  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Gary Ball, a co-owner of Medical Data Systems, has flown since he was sixteen. After moving to Florida, he and his wife Susan built a country home in Ontario to spend time with their growing family. They wanted it to feel long established, using reclaimed wood and furniture made to look antique.\n\nThe couple also opened their home for the Ladies of the Lake Luncheon in 2018. Guests supplied food or contributed to Community Living of Trent Highlands, raising more than $1,500. Gary and Susan matched the donations, doubling the money raised for the charity.",
    "html": "<p>Gary Ball, a co-owner of Medical Data Systems, has flown since he was sixteen. After moving to Florida, he and his wife Susan built a country home in Ontario to spend time with their growing family. They wanted it to feel long established, using reclaimed wood and furniture made to look antique.</p>\r\n<p>The couple also opened their home for the Ladies of the Lake Luncheon in 2018. Guests supplied food or contributed to Community Living of Trent Highlands, raising more than $1,500. Gary and Susan matched the donations, doubling the money raised for the charity.</p>\r\n",
